title":"I wrote a music player (2022)","url":"https://www.omarpolo.com/post/amused.html","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"dzwdz","user_is_author":false,"tags":["openbsd","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtsgzs","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtsgzs/i_wrote_music_player_2022"},{"short_id":"opogns","created_at":"2026-07-27T09:24:58.947-05:00","title":"Building a Fast Lock-Free Queue in Modern C++ From Scratch","url":"https://blog.jaysmito.dev/blog/04-fast-lockfree-queues/","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"LolPython","user_is_author":false,"tags":["c++","performance"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/opogns","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/opogns/building_fast_lock_free_queue_modern_c"},{"short_id":"yhzvzk","created_at":"2026-07-27T09:18:30.467-05:00","title":"Zstandard Worked Example (2022)","url":"https://nigeltao.github.io/blog/2022/zstandard-part-1-concepts.html","score":2,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"LeahNeukirchen","user_is_author":false,"tags":["compsci"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/yhzvzk","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/yhzvzk/zstandard_worked_example_2022"},{"short_id":"mqazme","created_at":"2026-07-27T08:44:42.332-05:00","title":"Would you like to see a “fork” of current tech as a whole?","url":"","score":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":13,"description":"\u003cp\u003eThe use of the word “fork” is intentional. I’m not talking of a Neo-Luddite reaction or pure tech nostalgia. The question is if current technologies in themselves are OK, but you’d rather like to see different uses to it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne example are LLMs: they could definitely be used for smaller things like spell checking or to actual work if they were biased towards proper citation and attribution instead of mere plagiarism. I’m not sure if the latter is possible so that’s one thing to be discussed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoreover, I didn’t ask “how” in the title as that would be a leading question, but if you have any ideas on how to do it, I would love to hear them.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"The use of the word “fork” is intentional. I’m not talking of a Neo-Luddite reaction or pure tech nostalgia. The question is if current technologies in themselves are OK, but you’d rather like to see different uses to it.\r\n\r\nOne example are LLMs: they could definitely be used for smaller things like spell checking or to actual work if they were biased towards proper citation and attribution instead of mere plagiarism. I’m not sure if the latter is possible so that’s one thing to be discussed.\r\n\r\nMoreover, I didn’t ask “how” in the title as that would be a leading question, but if you have any ideas on how to do it, I would love to hear them.","submitter_user":"tmcb","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","culture"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mqazme","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/mqazme/would_you_like_see_fork_current_tech_as"},{"short_id":"yijxwe","created_at":"2026-07-27T08:34:39.432-05:00","title":"Blogging Can Just Be Stating The Obvious","url":"https://blog.jim-nielsen.com/2026/blogging-stating-the-obvious/","score":48,"flags":0,"comment_count":6,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"rmoff","user_is_author":false,"tags":["education"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/yijxwe","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/yijxwe/blogging_can_just_be_stating_obvious"},{"short_id":"vtev1n","created_at":"2026-07-27T07:32:24.785-05:00","title":"How is the Bun Rewrite in Rust Going?","url":"https://lockwood.dev/ai/2026/07/27/how-is-the-bun-rewrite-in-rust-going.html","score":34,"flags":2,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"FedericoSchonborn","user_is_author":false,"tags":["vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/vtev1n","comments_url":"htt